ffects of electromagnetic field emitted by cellular phones on the EEG during a memory task</article-title><source>NeuroReport</source><year>2000</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>761</fpage><lpage>764</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10757515</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001756-200003200-00021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Papageorgiou</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Nanou</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsiafakis</surname><given-names>VG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapareliotis</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kontoangelos</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Capsalis</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabavilas</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Soldatos</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute mobile phone effects on pre-attentive operation</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2006</year><volume>397</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>103</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16406308</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2005.12.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>GUARD projects</collab></person-group><article-title>"Potential Adverse Effects of GSM Cellular Phones on Hearing"</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.guard.polimi.it"/></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sliwinska-Kowalska</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zmyslony</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dudarewicz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>No effects of acute exposure to the electromagnetic field emitted by mobile phones on brainstem auditory potentials in young volunteers</article-title><source>Int J Occup Med Environ Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14587532</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>